FX.08 — "CAPABILITIES DEAL THROUGH ONE SLOT". Built 05.-06.08.2026, measured,
and culled on 06.08.2026 in favour of the laid-out rack that ships now. Kept
because it worked and the argument against it was a design call, not a defect:
six capability modules dealt through one bay held at the middle of the window,
sticky stage carrying the heading with it, five modules parked (opacity 0,
inert, aria-hidden) at any moment, 3833px of runway for a section the grid now
gives in 1005px. What it lost on was reading: a visitor could never see MOTION
and GRAPHICS at once to compare them.

Worth reading even if it never comes back — the deck is where these were found
and written down:

  * the bay measured off the tallest module instead of guessed (--deck-bay),
    and why the measurement has to zero the property before it reads
  * the hold beat: six units of timeline for six modules, five hand-overs plus
    one empty beat, or the last module finishes arriving in the frame the stage
    lets go and is never seen at rest
  * the seated-module index divided by the timeline's unit count, not by the
    number of hand-overs
  * onRefresh re-parking, without which module 4 jumped back out mid-scrub

THIS PATCH APPLIES TO COMMIT 61ffdc5, NOT TO THE CURRENT TREE. It is the whole
working diff as it stood that morning, so it also carries the pnpm launch.json
fix, the SmoothScroll resize refresh and the AccentScroll needle note — all of
which are in the tree already and will collide if applied on top.

    git worktree add ../nullpunkt-fx08 61ffdc5
    cd ../nullpunkt-fx08
    git apply ../nullpunkt/scripts/fx08-one-bay-deck.patch

Read it there; delete the worktree when done (git worktree remove).

